{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>רוח, לב</b> — two words joined. The meaning: רוח איש יסבול חליו — a man's spirit sustains his illness, and the bodily qualities [are sustained] — and this is the rational spirit; wisdom sustains the anxieties." "<b>ורוח נכאה</b> — this is the one that grieves and grows angry over the vanities of the world, when it does not attain them. משקל נכאה — a weight of grief, full." "<b>מי ישאנה</b> — when it is suffering, for it carries the body, even though it is borne within it. And this suffering spirit does not learn wisdom, but a discerning heart that endures its affliction will acquire knowledge through its discernment."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:30.808851817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}